     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>i am new to ggplot2 and tried hard to get a plot the way i like.\r<br>The data srda looks like this:\r<br>    Thresh Time Color Intens Seen        rFit        gFit\r<br>1        1    0   RED    0.8    1  0.11033208  1.94633102\r<br>2        1    2   RED    0.2    1  0.01516950  1.69396036\r<br>3        1    3   RED   -0.4    1 -0.02895994  1.57692931\r<br>4        1    4   RED   -1.0    1 -0.07093717  1.46560594\r<br>8        1    8   RED   -1.0    1 -0.21934788  1.07202154\r<br>11       1   11   RED   -1.2    1 -0.31271811  0.82440417\r<br>15       1   16   RED   -1.2    1 -0.44033896  0.48595437\r<br>\r<br>The final code i came up with is:\r<br>p &lt;- ggplot(srda)\r<br>p &lt;- p + scale_x_continuous(name=&quot;Time (ms)&quot;,limits=c(0, 650))\r<br>p &lt;- p + scale_y_continuous(name=&quot;Intensity (cd * m^-2)&quot;,limits=c\r<br>(-10,3))\r<br>p &lt;- p + geom_point(aes(Time,Intens,colour=Color))\r<br>p &lt;- p + geom_line(aes(Time,rFit,colour=&quot;RED&quot;))\r<br>p &lt;- p + geom_line(aes(Time,gFit,colour=&quot;GREEN&quot;))\r<br>tt &lt;- data.frame(x=400,y=2,text=paste(&quot;Red target threshold: &quot;, coef\r<br>(rnls)[&quot;B&quot;], &quot;cd*s^-2&quot;,\r<br>\t&quot;\\nGreen target threshold: &quot;, coef(gnls)[&quot;B&quot;], &quot;cd*s^-2&quot;))\r<br>p &lt;- p + geom_text(data=tt,aes(x=x,y=y,label=text))\r<br>p\r<br>\r<br>Using scale_y_continuous the axis label is not centered on the y-axis\r<br>but centered at the hight of the label of the x-axis in the lower left\r<br>corner. Why?\r<br>\r<br>Using geom_text i would like to a) select a different font size and b)\r<br>have &quot;cd*s^-2&quot; nicely printed with superscript.\r<br>\r<br>I appreciate any help!\r<br>Thanks, Herbert"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
