     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><br><div><div>On Apr 12, 2009, at 3:58 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">herbert...@uni-tuebingen.de</a> wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><br>Hi,<br><br>i am new to ggplot2 and tried hard to get a plot the way i like.<br>The data srda looks like this:<br>    Thresh Time Color Intens Seen        rFit        gFit<br>1        1    0   RED    0.8    1  0.11033208  1.94633102<br>2        1    2   RED    0.2    1  0.01516950  1.69396036<br>3        1    3   RED   -0.4    1 -0.02895994  1.57692931<br>4        1    4   RED   -1.0    1 -0.07093717  1.46560594<br>8        1    8   RED   -1.0    1 -0.21934788  1.07202154<br>11       1   11   RED   -1.2    1 -0.31271811  0.82440417<br>15       1   16   RED   -1.2    1 -0.44033896  0.48595437<br><br>The final code i came up with is:<br>p &lt;- ggplot(srda)<br>p &lt;- p + scale_x_continuous(name=&quot;Time (ms)&quot;,limits=c(0, 650))<br>p &lt;- p + scale_y_continuous(name=&quot;Intensity (cd * m^-2)&quot;,limits=c<br>(-10,3))<br>p &lt;- p + geom_point(aes(Time,Intens,colour=Color))<br>p &lt;- p + geom_line(aes(Time,rFit,colour=&quot;RED&quot;))<br>p &lt;- p + geom_line(aes(Time,gFit,colour=&quot;GREEN&quot;))<br>tt &lt;- data.frame(x=400,y=2,text=paste(&quot;Red target threshold: &quot;, coef<br>(rnls)[&quot;B&quot;], &quot;cd*s^-2&quot;,<br><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>&quot;\\nGreen target threshold: &quot;, coef(gnls)[&quot;B&quot;], &quot;cd*s^-2&quot;))<br>p &lt;- p + geom_text(data=tt,aes(x=x,y=y,label=text))<br>p<br><br>Using scale_y_continuous the axis label is not centered on the y-axis<br>but centered at the hight of the label of the x-axis in the lower left<br>corner. Why?<br><br>Using geom_text i would like to a) select a different font size and b)<br>have &quot;cd*s^-2&quot; nicely printed with superscript.<br><br>I appreciate any help!<br>Thanks, Herbert<br><br><br></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>"
